      "spam": false,
      "value": "I too wish for this to be a thing but unfortunately there isn't an API to actually get that data in the current version of unity (without scraping the the editor log which I don't think is a good idea), though I have heard there is such an API in unity 2018 so whenever we switch to that this can be looked into properly.\n\nI will leave you with this, https://docs.unity3d.com/560/Documentation/Manual/ReducingFilesize.html, it describes the output found in the editor log as well as tips on how to reduce the build size.\n\nAlso here's a similar canny request that might be worth upvoting as well, https://vrchat.canny.io/feature-requests/p/sdk-build-time-optimization-notifications",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-03-07T09:46:14.697Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Can the SDK show avatar and world bundle size and breakdown of contents after building, as logged in Unity's editor log? That way people can get a sense of what they're uploading and how it's packaged",
